/* =====================================================================================
   DM-A1  |  Attribute Checks - Data Type & Format Preserved
   Dates, decimals and trailing spaces not truncated or altered on load. Pass criterion: types & formats match source (no FAIL rows; REVIEW rows explained as documented exceptions).

   Check ID: DM-A1
   Category: Attribute checks
   Sign-off criterion: Data type & format preserved
   Method: (a) column type compare: every RAW column feeding a satellite column
       (lineage generated from the models) vs the satellite column, from INFORMATION_SCHEMA
       -- type, length, precision, scale, fractional seconds; (b) sample trace: for 1:1
       mapped columns, the vault value vs the RAW value on the agreed sample, classified as
       exact / trimmed / re-formatted / decimals lost / truncated / different
   Pass criteria / tolerance: Types & formats match source
   Owner: LUMIQ
   Vault location: BAGIC_PREPROD_CURATED_DB.BGIL_DATA_MODEL
   Maximus RAW: BAGIC_PROD_MIRROR_DB.MAXI_RAW
   Opus RAW (test): BAGIC_PREPROD_CURATED_DB.UTILS (prod:
       BAGIC_PROD_MIRROR_DB.OPUS_GG_DWHSTAGE)
   Scope: Every satellite model of maximus_partner_dv_dbt and opus_partner_dv_dbt
       (standard + augmented). Satellite tables are shared; rows are scoped by
       RECORD_SOURCE prefix (MAXIMUS / OPUS).
   Sample (query b): 100 (hash key, RECORD_SOURCE) units per satellite, chosen
       deterministically by md5(hash key | record source | 'DM-A') so every re-run reads
       the same units. Change SAMPLE_SIZE in the generator to agree a different sample.
   Session settings (query b): Run the ALTER SESSION first: timestamps rendered with 9
       fractional digits so a value stored as text with fewer digits shows as truncated.
   transform_flags: TRIM / BLANK->NULL / UPPER: text cleaned on load; SCALE0: integer
       cast (try_to_number / ::number without scale); TO_TIMESTAMP / TO_DATE: type
       conversion; COALESCE / CASE: derived from several RAW columns; SAT_VARCHAR:
       sat_multi_source stores the payload as VARCHAR
   Known design exceptions: Layer-1 staging trims every text column and turns blanks
       into NULL (nullif(trim(...), '')), so trailing spaces are NOT preserved by design.
       Opus staging casts DATE / TIMESTAMP to TIMESTAMP_NTZ. These show as 'PASS (... by
       design)' / REVIEW and must be accepted by BGIL as documented exceptions or fixed.
   Output columns: (a) sat_column, sat_type, raw_table, raw_column, raw_type,
       transform_flags, type_verdict, transform; (b) sat_column, compared, exact,
       trimmed_or_blank_to_null, typed_value_kept_text_differs, reformatted, decimals_lost,
       truncated, different_value, format_status

   GENERATED by validation/tools/gen_dm_a.py from the current dbt models -- edit the generator,
   not this file. The queries are IDENTICAL to those in the matching .docx.

   Revision notes:
   - Generated 2026-10-12 from the current opus_partner_dv_dbt and maximus_partner_dv_dbt
     models by validation/tools/gen_dm_a.py; results are blank and must be filled in
     after running the queries.
   - Scope: 98 MAXIMUS + 59 OPUS satellite models = 157 sections (141 single-active, 12
     multi-active, 4 object-column sats; 15 fed by an Opus stitch view).
   - Lineage is parsed, not typed: sat -> stg2 stage / wrapper / unpivot / stitch ->
     layer-1 stg_ -> RAW column. Hash keys reproduced as automate_dv 0.11.5 does:
     MD5_BINARY(NULLIF(UPPER(TRIM(CAST(<NK> AS VARCHAR))), '')).
   - Static finding: 58 satellite column(s) are loaded through an integer cast
     (try_to_number / ::number without scale); query (a) of DM-A1 reports DECIMALS LOST
     where the RAW column has a scale.
   - Lineage warnings (stage column excluded by src_column_map): 0.
   ===================================================================================== */


